  [1mProposed design[0m

  - Stay in plain HTML/CSS/JS inside [38;5;153mindex.html[39m — matching what's there. No dependencies, no build step.
  - Markup: each item is a [38;5;153m<li>[39m in a [38;5;153m<ul>[39m inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m, containing a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox" id="...">[39m plus a
    [38;5;153m<label for="...">[39m. Native input means keyboard and screen-reader behavior come for free.
  - State: the checkbox's own [38;5;153mchecked[39m property is the state. A small [38;5;153mchange[39m listener toggles a [38;5;153mdone[39m class on the row so
    checked items render struck-through/dimmed. No persistence across reloads.
  - Since [38;5;153m<main>[39m is currently empty, I'll seed it with two or three example items so the checkbox is actually visible —
    say the word if you'd rather I add the markup for exactly one item.
  - Testing: no test setup exists in this repo, so verification is manual — open the page, click a checkbox, confirm it
    toggles and the strikethrough follows. I won't add a test framework unless you want one.

  [1mThe one fork worth naming:[0m hardcoded [38;5;153m<li>[39m markup versus a small JS helper that renders checkbox rows from an array.
  Hardcoded is fewer moving parts and reads clearly for a handful of items; the helper buys you adding items
  programmatically later but is more machinery than "nothing fancy" implies. I recommend hardcoded markup — converting
  to a render helper later is cheap and touches only this one file.

